WEBVTT

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.940
<b>Get Pablo's Collection</b>

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.080
Lupin, you're meant to sing that song 
<i>before </i>New Year's Day, not on it.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.080
Don't be such a stickler for detail.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:58.000
You're the one who wanted to celebrate 
New Year's properly for once.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.460
It is ready.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.230
Red bean mochi, huh?

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.660
Nice.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.760
You've got it all wrong, Goemon.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.470
The paste's meant to be smooth, not lumpy.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.310
No.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.980
The only true red bean paste is...

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.850
...coarse!

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.710
I like mine chunky, to be honest.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.300
A coin? No, a medal...

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.520
Did you guys forget?

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.820
This is from the Pablo Collection.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.630
I'm talking about the Pablo Collection!

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.880
The South American drug kingpin?

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:46.350
Thing is, Lupin, Pablo was getting on in years,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.760
and nobody's seen him 
since his disappearance.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.880
Even the existence of such 
a "collection" is only a rumor.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:56.100
Rumor? Sour grapes from the saps who 
couldn't sniff out the goodies, more like.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.560
Satellite pics?

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.840
Get a load of this.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.580
P-A-B... Pablo?

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.740
And there you have it.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.480
Things tend to get kinda hairy 
in that part of South America...

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:14.420
It sure would be handy to have a big, 
strong fella like Goemon helpin' me out!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.740
Understood.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:19.170
Don't bother asking me any 
obvious questions, pal.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.670
That settles it, then.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.070
Now we're just waiting on...

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.310
Lupin!

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.180
Here I am.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:28.990
Fujiko?

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:31.570
Hey! Why the hell is <i>she</i> coming with us?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.070
I mentioned it in passing, you see, 
and she <i>insisted </i>on tagging along.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.690
This is the last stop before 
we're knee-deep in jungle.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.720
Buy whatever you're gonna need.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.840
Where's Fujiko?

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.520
Getting some local intel.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:59.850
Say, is there a map of the 
area you could let me have?

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:04.850
No maps. Makes the 
cartels mad. This is their turf.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.590
I'm not even from around here.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.430
I've got nothing to do with the cartels.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.330
W-Well, I suppose what they 
don't know won't hurt them...

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.460
Thank you <i>so</i> much!

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:22.110
Looks like the deadly power 
of the cleavage knows no borders.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.620
Your drinks are on the house, too.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:25.710
Really?!

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.920
Sure. And take some for the road.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.870
You're such a sweetheart!

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:36.590
Whoa!

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:39.770
Man, couldn't we have 
just chartered a boat?

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.220
Unfortunately, that wasn't an option.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.080
We had international affairs to consider.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.310
The Pablo Collection is on
 the very edge of the jungle.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:54.960
Lake El Elquele is near it, and both Borazil 
and Baraguay have staked claims on it.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.570
Which means river travel
 invites a lot of scrutiny.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.230
So making our way there
over land is safer all round.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.380
Is everything safe down here, too?

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.200
No, Lupin.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.080
Whoopsy-daisy!

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.070
Oh, Fujicakes, I'm trying to drive here.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:18.050
Honestly...

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.550
Oh, dear. Here come more road hazards!

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.770
Oh, how <i>dangerous!</i>

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:22.900
Hey!

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.020
Lupin!

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.370
Just a few road hazards, 
Fujicakes. That's all.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.910
Good grief. If he could just 
keep it in his pants...

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.010
You're heavy, Jigen.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:46.840
Lupin...

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.780
No peeking, okay?

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.280
I'll be sitting here and waiting! Woof!

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.600
That explains why she bought 
so much damn water.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.740
What's up?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.030
I shall practice my swing.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.570
I get where you're coming from...

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.540
Lupin!

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:06.500
What's up?

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.790
We're gonna go stretch our legs 
for a bit. Hold the fort, will ya?

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:11.150
Yeah, sure, whatever.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.160
Say, Lupin... Who were those 
people in the village?

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.840
You noticed them, huh?

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:20.820
Sure did.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.310
Probably some of Pablo's old cronies.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.570
I thought the Pablo Family disbanded.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.650
All the more reason for 
them to chase his fortune,

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.720
so they can get the gang back together.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:42.080
Say what?! Fujiko!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.570
Did you get him?

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.540
Yeah. I'm sure of it.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.550
Stay sharp. There were more of them.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.860
There they are! Lupin's gang!

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:58.710
I see him!

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:01.430
Light him up!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.600
E-Enough of this! Pull out for now!

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:12.900
You okay, Fujiko?

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:16.990
Oh, please. I saw that ambush coming 
a mile away. Where are the bad guys?

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.740
Jigen and Goemon are out there, 
so I'm sure there's no need to worry.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:22.880
I see...

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:34.270
Damn! Curse that Lupin.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:38.280
Let's give it up. 
There's no way we can beat them.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.080
If we take them on by ourselves, no.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.730
This village has a phone, right?

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:47.480
Get Commander Gomez of the 
Borazillian Navy on the line.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.380
Ugh, I'm so tired!

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.610
Maybe you oughta dress 
for the terrain next time.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:05.420
That's rich, coming from a man 
who wears the same suit all the time.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.910
This one was made specifically for 
summer. Different material.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.690
Fujicakes...

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.910
Should I give you a piggyback ride?

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:13.720
No.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.700
Not with that look in your eye.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:17.490
Look.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.300
A submarine?

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.260
Awfully <i>small</i>...

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.160
A Kittredge K-350.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:51.950
Couldn't ask for a better ride if you're 
trying to get somewhere unnoticed.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.430
I wonder what's in the 
drug kingpin's fortune!

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.400
No clue.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.800
But they say Pablo was making 
7 billion bucks a day in the drug trade,

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:11.000
so there's no telling what 
he did with that kinda cash.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.950
Well, ain't that something?

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.950
Did you find the loot?

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:32.210
Yeah. Pablo has one hell of a collection!

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:35.410
These are...

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.970
Yep!

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.740
This is the Pablo Collection.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:45.170
Get a load of this! A Bugatti Type 57 Tank,

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:48.150
a Delahaye 175S Roadster...

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.820
Damn, he even has a Rolls-Royce 15 hp!

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.600
This is some car show.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.190
Indeed.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.440
And in such good condition...

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.690
I get the feeling me and 
their owner would get along.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:05.150
This is so stupid. They're just 
a bunch of oversized minicars.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.710
Oh, no, Ms. Fujiko...

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.790
Sell these to the right enthusiast 
and they'll net you a tidy sum.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:10.580
How much exactly?

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:14.180
Well, that one, probably around
 2.5 mill, and that one...

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.260
I couldn't even guesstimate!

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.670
You should've said so sooner, Lupin!

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:22.780
So how do we get them out of here?

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.670
Now, hold your horses!

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.490
First things first...

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:31.950
Who's there?

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:52.950
Move!

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.090
Son of a...

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.590
What the hell?!

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.890
Pretty sure I aimed for the tires...

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.240
Leave this to me.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.560
Impossible!

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.600
Looks like your luck's as bad as mine, Goemon.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.680
How about a race, then?

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.110
Fujiko! You're on checkered flag duty!

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.360
Lupin?

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:27.060
What checkered flag?

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:41.960
Not bad...

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:05.880
What the heck is he thinking?

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.340
What do you see?

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.050
It's the name!

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:17.490
The "Pablo" carved out of the 
jungle was actually a race track.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.590
I bet you're enjoying this, too...

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:46.440
Who won?!

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.020
Lupin, obviously!

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:59.070
What a nice ride.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.850
You took good care of your cars...

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.540
...drug kingpin, Pablo.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.470
What the... What happened?

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:31.150
What does it look like? The spell wore off.

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:32.820
Then, what about the collection?

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.340
If you take it to a scrapyard, 
you might get 500 bucks out of it.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:39.340
No way!

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:44.080
But... But not every single 
one of them is scrap, right?!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:51.850
I'll be taking this, though...

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.010
Señor Pablo.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.900
What?! What now?

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:07.020
That's a ship's guns...

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.940
Why would the navy be after us?

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.410
When all else fails, flee.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:19.980
Don't worry. We're just 
trying to scare them.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:24.630
More importantly, you've confirmed the 
existence of the Pablo Collection, right?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.910
Lupin <i>himself</i> is here.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.870
You can rest assured that it's real, sir.

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:31.670
<i>You didn't mention that I was shelling Lupin...</i>

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.490
I think we're looking at a 70-30 split here.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.760
<i>If you can't accept 50-50...</i>

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:39.110
<i>I can always report you to your superiors.</i>

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:42.710
<i>"The commander went after the 
collection without telling you."</i>

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:49.220
When you're a crook, you tend to take 
these types of deals very seriously, sir.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:56.700
Can't we just tell them, 
"The collection's a bunch of scrap"?

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:00.450
It's not scrap. It's got <i>sentimental</i> value.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:04.760
Besides, it's not like they'd believe us 
even if we could get a message to them.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.700
So what are we going to do, then?

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:10.630
Because I am <i>not </i>taking on an armed force.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:11.930
It'll be fine.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.900
See?

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.770
I see. If we travel underwater...

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.260
Well? Can you get it running?

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:22.570
It's been kept in good condition.

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:26.520
The only thing missing 
is a beautiful stewardess.

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:29.510
Do you really need one 
if I'm going to be in there?

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.830
There's one problem with 
that, unfortunately.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.070
Fujicakes, how much do you weigh?

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.480
That's not a question you ask a lady.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:41.040
You wanna save the flirting 
for after we've made our escape?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.670
No, listen...

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:46.550
This thing was built for two people, 
maybe three at a push.

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:47.890
Which means...

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:51.050
Well, then! They <i>do</i> say "Ladies first"—

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:54.560
No such saying exists in my country.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:59.680
Lupin, if you hadn't brought Fujiko along,
we could've all gotten in that thing!

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.580
Oh, quit whining.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:04.290
Let's just draw lots. Nice and impersonal.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.250
I refuse.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.830
I am in no doubt that you have 
somehow tampered with the lots.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.520
Where's the trust?

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:13.690
How about rock, paper, scissors, then?

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.440
Winner takes all.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:16.830
Very well.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:20.580
I'm throwing scissors, 
so you all throw paper, okay?

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:21.960
'Kay!

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:23.580
Let's do this!

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.820
Rock... paper...

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:27.050
T-Time out!

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.610
What?! We're in the middle of something here...

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.980
Sorry! I need the little thieves' room.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.400
I can't hold it!

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:39.000
You know that leaks and submarines 
don't go together, right?

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.580
Just go already!

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.720
Gotta pee, gotta pee, gotta pee...

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:51.820
Now, let's see here...

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:00.590
Tch, cut off by land, sea, and air, huh?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.120
So be it.

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:08.410
I figure I'm the only guy in the world who 
could make it out of this kind of mess.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:24.120
If I manage to disguise myself as one of them,
 I should be able to pull this off.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:25.730
Over there! It's Lupin's gang!

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.020
Say what?!

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.770
That makes eight.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:39.820
It's me, dude, <i>me</i>!

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:42.190
Lupin? What are you doing here?

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:44.540
I should be asking <i>you </i>that!

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:49.080
You could search the world over and find no 
man capable of breaking through this siege,

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.750
other than myself.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.600
You stupid samurai!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.390
Keep shooting! Don't let them get close!

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:02.750
I'm just about the only guy who can triumph 
over this kind of adversity, don't you think?

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.970
Jigen... you...

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:05.650
Over there!

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:10.440
A marksman making idle chitchat... How foolish.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.900
I saved your asses, y'know!

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:16.970
You two should buzz off! 
I'll figure something out!

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:20.290
I believe the two of you should leave.
 I shall handle this matter.

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:22.660
You might as well run off 
with Fujiko, Lupin!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.790
I don't like what you're implying, bub!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.580
Are you two hard of 
hearing? Leave this to—

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:25.580
What don't you like about it?!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.580
You got a problem with me?!

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.430
Dammit!

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:31.480
We're trying to have a conversation 
here! Cut out that racket!

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.730
We'd better shut them up first, then.

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:34.910
Understood!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:50.400
And, in the end, he went and 
chose his friends over me!

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:55.190
Aw, hell no!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.820
Lupin, you dummy!

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.840
It's been a week...

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:19.580
I'm pretty sure this is the rendezvous spot.

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.110
But no one's shown...

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.610
Oh man, that bit with the bridge was tough.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:26.840
Lupin?

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:29.000
They even had a tank waiting for us!

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:32.090
Yeah, that part had me freaking out.

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:36.310
There's no telling what would have become 
of us if you hadn't had your idea, Lupin.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:38.950
Hey, we only pulled it off 
thanks to you, Master Goemon.

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:43.200
I know I told you to do it, but I didn't think 
you'd actually be able to slice through a tank.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.190
I thought we were dead meat when 
that chopper showed up, though.

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:49.190
Me, too, actually!

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.970
As did I.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:53.800
What? We all thought that?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:58.430
Men can be such children.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.070
Ack! Too hot!

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:04.270
I seriously have the best pals in the world.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:06.630
You're not so bad, yourself...

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:12.040
Time really flies...

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.660
How long has it been since that escapade?

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:17.000
I don't even wanna think about it.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.600
There is one thing I feel needs addressing.

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.490
What's that?

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:26.170
If I remember correctly, 
Jigen was the first of us to flee.

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:29.200
It wasn't me! It was Lupin!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:32.960
Aw, Grandpa, your memories 
must be all jumbled up again.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.500
You're not that much younger than me!

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.930
Quit acting like I'm ancient!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:40.300
My memories are certain. 
There is no doubt in my mind.

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:40.450
Goemon, stop spouting that crap!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.510
Let's just chalk it up to your twilight 
years dimming your memory.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.770
Shut the hell up!

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:42.800
I am positive.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:43.770
You two...

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:44.370
Jigen...

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:45.740
...need to shut up!

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:20.780
Goemon Ishikawa is attending 
some sort of anime event?

00:22:20.780 --> 00:22:23.640
The nerve of the guy, thinking 
he can sneak past me unnoticed!

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:25.900
Apparently, he plans on 
robbing a multimillionaire

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:28.160
by blending in with a crowd of cosplayers.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:31.600
You should never have sent 
Goemon in by himself, Lupin!

00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:37.580
He's got the same weakness he's always had:
 he loses his cool around women!

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:41.090
Next time: The Extravagance 
of Goemon Ishikawa XIII

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:44.910
<b>The Extravagance of Goemon Ishikawa XIII</b>

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:43.760
I have to say, he really doesn't 
blend in on the streets of France.
